{t:'Blue-chip Impressionist & Modern estates',dir:'heat',p:'Monet’s Iris made €50m ($56m) after six bidders competed for 45 minutes, the highest nominal auction price in France, and the Schlumberger sale made €74.4m against a €40m estimate with every lot sold; the winning bid came through Sotheby’s Asia. Christie’s made £218.6m in two London evening sales, led by Kandinsky (£31.6m) and Mondrian (£25.2m). November brings Sotheby’s $450m Blaquier-Arrieta group with a Van Gogh at about $180m and a $60–80m Kandinsky at Christie’s. Impressionist & Modern auction sales rose 133% in the first half (Bank of America), back to about their 2022 level.',s:[['TAN: Monet €50m','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/23/monets-monumental-iris-makes-56m-in-paris'],['TAN: Christie’s London','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/15/christies-achieves-%c2%a3219m-in-steady-solid-london-sales'],['TAN: $450m collection','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/09/30/450m-impressionist-collectionincluding-a-potentially-record-breaking-van-gogh-paintingto-be-sold-at-sothebys-new-york'],['Khaleej Times: Kandinsky','https://www.khaleejtimes.com/uae/christies-brings-dh477m-in-art-to-abu-dhabi-for-auction'],['BofA Fall 2026','https://www.privatebank.bankofamerica.com/articles/art-market-fall-update.html']]},
{t:'Ultra-contemporary and young artists',dir:'cool',p:'Artprice counts fine-art auction sales up 41% for July 2025–June 2026 but contemporary only 6%, with artists under 40 down 26.6%; Bank of America puts young contemporary 88% below its 2022 peak. Sotheby’s London contemporary evening sale made £45.9m, below last October’s £47.6m, with hammer short of the low estimate and a Kusama at £320,000 against a £1m low estimate. Phillips’ records for Pade (£167,700) and Yaeger (£645,000) show demand for chosen names, not for the segment.',s:[['Artprice release','https://chainwire.org/2026/10/08/artprice-releases-its-33rd-annual-contemporary-art-market-report-for-2026-record-transactions-price-trends-the-balance-of-market-power-and-artists-from-the-global-south'],['BofA fall update','https://www.privatebank.bankofamerica.com/articles/art-market-fall-update.html?sf278602346=1'],['TAN: Sotheby’s London','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/16/de-kooning-sets-record-but-still-falls-flat-at-muted-sothebys-contemporary-evening-sale'],['We Wealth: Phillips','https://www.we-wealth.com/news/phillips-risultati-asta-londra-frieze-banksy-richter']]},
{t:'Paris: political risk enters the calendar',dir:'cool',p:'Art Basel Paris shut its 211-exhibitor fair at 7pm on 23 October and lost two of its three public days, while the Louvre, Orsay, Grand Palais and several blue-chip galleries closed on 24 October as about 70,000 police deployed nationwide. Dealing was front-loaded into the new 20 October Avant Première and the previews (Richter $10.5m at Hauser & Wirth, Mehretu $7.8m at White Cube), so sales held up better than footfall, which was 73,000 in 2025. Organisers and dealers now have to price event risk into Paris week.',s:[['TAN: early closure','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/22/art-basel-paris-closes-early-due-to-protests'],['TAN: sales despite riots','https://theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/21/riots-do-not-deter-big-ticket-sales-at-art-basel-paris'],['AP: closures and policing','https://www.bostonglobe.com/2026/10/23/world/french-police-prepare-saturday-protests-louvre-closed/'],['AFP: 73,000 in 2025','https://malaymail.com/news/life/2026/10/23/picasso-basquiat-and-an-early-exit-art-basel-paris-shuts-ahead-of-weekend-demos/240254']]},
{t:'London’s recovery holds',dir:'heat',p:'Sotheby’s London has passed $1bn in 2026, with Modern and contemporary at £598m, its best year to date since 2015, and Christie’s 20th/21st Century sale (£111.1m) edged past October 2025’s £106.9m. Phillips sold all 20 lots for £14.8m, up 44%. At Frieze London (172 galleries) dealers said the top and bottom were selling but decisions were slower in between.',s:[['TAN: Sotheby’s London','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/16/de-kooning-sets-record-but-still-falls-flat-at-muted-sothebys-contemporary-evening-sale'],['TAN: Christie’s London','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/15/christies-achieves-%c2%a3219m-in-steady-solid-london-sales'],['We Wealth: Phillips','https://www.we-wealth.com/news/phillips-risultati-asta-londra-frieze-banksy-richter'],['TAN: Frieze London','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/15/frieze-london-buyers-taking-risks-others-are-taking-their-time']]},
{t:'Private sales, guarantees and fees',dir:'heat',p:'Christie’s private sales passed $1bn and Sotheby’s $826m (+52%, record) by mid-year. Blaquier-Arrieta is house-guaranteed with irrevocable bids being syndicated; Christie’s Kandinsky carries a third-party guarantee and its Klimt is guaranteed; the Peter Simon collection was guaranteed lot by lot and made £107.5m, 40 of 41 sold; in Paris, Il Sole 24 Ore reported that the guarantors may have bought five of the eight guaranteed Durand-Ruel lots; six of the 16 Weiss bankruptcy lots at Sotheby’s carry house guarantees; Koons brings ≈$100m to Christie’s; Lévy Gorvy Dayan launched sealed single-lot auctions; all four major houses raised buyer’s fees in 2026 (28–29% at the lower tier).',s:[['Artnet: Blaquier-Arrieta','https://news.artnet.com/market/sothebys-blaquier-collection-van-gogh-cezanne-2816398'],['Bloomberg: Weiss at Sotheby’s','https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-09-30/bankrupt-fund-founder-weiss-agrees-to-auction-art-at-sotheby-s'],['Artnet: Koons at Christie’s','https://news.artnet.com/artnet-bulletin/jeff-koons-christies-oct-5-2819871'],['Artnet: fee rises','https://news.artnet.com/multimedia/art-market-minute-sep-28-2816786']]},
{t:'Art credit keeps growing',dir:'steady',p:'19% of HNW collectors plan to borrow against art in the next year (30% in the US) and about 20% already have; Bank of America’s art lending is growing 8–10% a year. Sotheby’s sold its second art-loan securitisation ($600m, AAA-rated senior notes) in January and refinanced with an $825m 2031 bond at about 8.5% in April. With guarantees on about 70% of New York evening-sale lots last November (Citi), credit and risk transfer now shape how the top of the market clears.',s:[['Art Basel & UBS survey','https://www.artbasel.com/stories/the-art-basel-and-ubs-survey-of-global-collecting-2026'],['BofA fall update','https://www.privatebank.bankofamerica.com/articles/art-market-fall-update.html?sf278602346=1'],['American Banker: $600m ABS','https://asreport.americanbanker.com/news/sothebys-to-raise-600-million-from-a-pool-of-art-loans'],['Il Sole 24 Ore: $825m bond','https://en.ilsole24ore.com/art/sotheby-s-restarts-but-debt-knot-not-untied-AIdkBcbC'],['Citi: guarantees','https://www.privatebank.citibank.com/doc/art/State-of-the-art-market-2026.pdf.coredownload.inline.pdf']]},
{t:'The Gulf: infrastructure, war-shadowed',dir:'heat',p:'Christie’s held its first Abu Dhabi fine-art auction on 1 November (70 works) and previewed over $130m of New York-bound art there; Sotheby’s adds its first Abu Dhabi fine-art sale on 10 December, and Frieze Abu Dhabi opens on 19 November with 84 galleries including Gagosian, Pace and Ropac. Artprice, however, puts Middle East auction sales down 28% for July 2025–June 2026, so the build-out is ahead of the numbers. Art Basel Qatar returns on 26–30 January 2027 after an 87-gallery debut.',s:[['The National: Christie’s CEO','https://thenationalnews.com/arts-culture/art-design/2026/10/30/abu-dhabi-is-gaining-ground-in-the-art-market-says-christies-ceo'],['Khaleej Times: $130m preview','https://www.khaleejtimes.com/uae/christies-brings-dh477m-in-art-to-abu-dhabi-for-auction'],['Gulf News: Sotheby’s Abu Dhabi','https://gulfnews.com/uae/abu-dhabi/sothebys-to-hold-first-international-fine-art-auction-in-abu-dhabi-1.500723894'],['TAN: Frieze Abu Dhabi','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/08/27/frieze-abu-dhabi-galleries-inaugural-fair'],['Artprice release','https://chainwire.org/2026/10/08/artprice-releases-its-33rd-annual-contemporary-art-market-report-for-2026-record-transactions-price-trends-the-balance-of-market-power-and-artists-from-the-global-south']]},
{t:'Younger, better-informed buyers, wary of unknowns',dir:'heat',p:'The Art Basel & UBS survey puts average HNW fine-art spending at $124,265 in 2025 (+13%) and Gen Z’s at $347,460, with 58% expecting growth over the next year and ArtTactic’s September confidence reading back in positive territory. Use of apps and AI tools rose to 22% from 4% in 2024, and Christie’s says 47% of its new clients are millennials or Gen Z. Yet 77% spent under $50,000 in H1 2026 and only 45% bought a newly discovered artist (66% in 2025).',s:[['Art Basel & UBS survey','https://www.artbasel.com/stories/the-art-basel-and-ubs-survey-of-global-collecting-2026'],['UBS release, 8 Oct','https://www.ubs.com/global/en/media/display-page-ndp/en-20261008-art-basel-ubs-survey.html'],['ArtTactic, Sept 2026','https://arttactic.com/reports/contemporary-art-market-confidence-report-september-2026'],['The National: Christie’s CEO','https://thenationalnews.com/arts-culture/art-design/2026/10/30/abu-dhabi-is-gaining-ground-in-the-art-market-says-christies-ceo']]},
{t:'Klimt and Vienna 1900',dir:'steady',p:'Portrait of Elisabeth Lederer made $236.4m (Sotheby’s, Lauder sale), the modern-art record, and Bildnis Gertrud Loew followed at £36.2m in June against a £20–30m estimate. Christie’s offers the Attersee landscape Litzlbergkeller (1915–16) at $60–80m on 17 November, guaranteed; it was bought at Sotheby’s New York in 1997 for $14.7m from the Serge Sabarsky estate.',s:[['ARTnews: Lederer record','https://www.artnews.com/art-news/news/gustav-klimt-portrait-of-elisabeth-lederer-auction-record-1234762083/'],['USA Art News: Litzlbergkeller','https://usaartnews.com/auctions/christies-to-offer-gustav-klimt-landscape-with-80-million-estimate/']]},
{t:'Old Masters at the top',dir:'heat',p:'Christie’s Old Masters made $183m in H1 2026 (+232%). A Roman marble torso made $34.3m against $8–12m at Sotheby’s New York on 21 October, an auction record for a Roman antiquity. Rubens’ Landscape with Willows nearly doubled its high estimate at HK$19.2m in Hong Kong (29 Sept). Turner’s Rome, from Mount Aventine returns at £50m on 9 December; Thomas Kaplan’s Leiden Collection paid £6.75m for a Rembrandt in December 2025.',s:[['USA Art News: Roman torso','https://usaartnews.com/auctions/roman-imperial-torso-sells-for-343-million-at-sothebys/'],['Artnet: Christie’s H1','https://news.artnet.com/market/christies-h1-mid-year-sales-2026-2788024'],['TAN: Rembrandt buyer','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/09/28/rembrandt-painting-buyer-revealed-leiden-collection-thomas-kaplan']]},
{t:'Women Surrealists',dir:'heat',p:'Kahlo’s El sueño set the $54.7m record for a woman artist (Nov 2025). Tanning’s Children’s Games made £4.7m and Toyen £3.7m at Christie’s London in March 2026. Annual sales of women Surrealists rose from $7.9m (2018) to $94.3m (2024).',s:[['Art Basel report note','https://www.artbasel.com/stories/art-market-report-london-female-surrealists-frida-kahlo?lang=en'],['ARTnews: Kahlo record','https://www.artnews.com/art-news/news/frida-kahlo-painting-sothebys-record-woman-surrealism-1234762747/']]},
{t:'Hong Kong and Asian buying',dir:'steady',p:'Volume up, share down. The autumn series reached ≈HK$2bn ($255m) against $165m in spring: Christie’s HK$956.5m (+17%), Sotheby’s HK$956m (91% sold), Phillips HK$94.5m; Christie’s drew 30% more young new buyers. But ArtTactic put H1 Hong Kong at $764m, a declining share next to London’s $1.42bn (+131%).',s:[['TAN: ArtTactic H1 2026','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/07/10/auction-houses-made-significant-recoveries-in-2026-arttactic-report-finds']]},
{t:'Luxury, watches, memorabilia, pop culture',dir:'heat',p:'Luxury collectibles rose 25% in H1 (ArtTactic); memorabilia +308% to $96.1m; Christie’s luxury $539m (+15%). Heritage made $1.41bn in H1 (+47%). Christie’s opened a pop-culture division (24 Sept) and scheduled a second anime sale. The Art Newspaper: under-40 buyers prize Pokémon ($16.5m card) over Picasso.',s:[['TAN: Poussin to Pokémon','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/09/10/from-poussin-and-pollock-to-pokemon-and-super-mario-bros-the-market-is-shifting'],['Hyperallergic: Christie’s pop culture','https://hyperallergic.com/christies-launches-pop-culture-division-to-court-millennial-and-gen-z-buyers/']]},
{t:'Gallery consolidation and fair downsizing',dir:'cool',p:'Art Basel Miami Beach (2–6 December) has 272 exhibitors on a floor about 12% smaller, with its main Galleries sector down to 204; Pace cut about 50 artists and 50 staff in June. Bank of America notes dealers still make more than half of global sales but face rising costs and selective demand, and the survey puts dealers at 42% of HNW spending including fairs. Frieze London grew to 172 galleries, so the squeeze is uneven.',s:[['Art Basel: Miami Beach 2026','https://www.artbasel.com/stories/art-basel-announces-exhibitors-and-a-reconfigured-showfloor-for-miami-beach-2026'],['Apollo: Pace cuts','https://apollo-magazine.com/?p=1044152'],['BofA fall update','https://www.privatebank.bankofamerica.com/articles/art-market-fall-update.html?sf278602346=1'],['Art Basel & UBS survey','https://www.artbasel.com/stories/the-art-basel-and-ubs-survey-of-global-collecting-2026'],['USA Art News: Frieze 172','https://usaartnews.com/news/frieze-london-returns-with-172-galleries-and-a-few-notable-absences']]},
{t:'Data, standards and the wealth transfer',dir:'steady',p:'The UK will standardise auction sales data with a new SIC code (47.921) as the trade weighs a sector-wide body. Deloitte expects about $1tn of art and collectibles to change hands by 2035; Bank of America cites the estimate as $992bn and reports that only 67% of heirs plan to keep inherited works. Artnet and Artsy merged under Beowolff Capital; Invaluable sold to Liquidity Services for $80m.',s:[['TAN: SIC code','https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/09/11/uk-moves-to-standardise-auction-sale-data-as-wider-sector-rallies-support-for-a-new-trade-body'],['Fortune: wealth transfer','https://fortune.com/2025/11/19/great-wealth-transfer-art-collections-boomers-millennials-dinosaur-skeletons']]}
